          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Solon's Reforms</strong><br>\nSolon, another Athenian statesman, emerged to reform Dracon's laws about a century later. He mitigated the severity of Dracon's laws, aiming for more proportionate justice. Solon's changes laid the foundation for democracy in Athens, easing the stringent penalties that had defined the older system.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Dracon's Legacy</strong><br>\nDracon's legacy lived on through his contribution to the concept of written law. His work paved the way for subsequent legal systems not only in Greece but also in other civilizations. Even though his laws were eventually deemed too harsh, they were crucial in the evolution of Greek legal proceedings.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Evaluating Dracon's Contribution</strong><br>\nEvaluating Dracon's contribution to history involves understanding the context of his times. While his laws now seem excessively harsh, they were important in moving away from the arbitrary rule of power to a system where laws governed public life. His codes were an early attempt at justice, albeit a rigid and unforgiving one.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
